00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.240
isometric exercise otherwise known as a

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:08.440
static hold has come up on top as the

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.639
best exercise to reduce blood pressure

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.519
even more so than other forms of

00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:15.440
exercise like running lifting weights

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:17.760
and a number of others and much to my

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:20.000
happiness multiple people asked on the

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.480
last video going over the clinical data

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
why isometric exercise has such a

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.519
profound impact so what's so unique

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.640
about isometric exercise that gives it

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:30.519
this significant blood pressure lowering

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.000
effect

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:35.360
in brief isometric exercise is literally

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.079
just holding a stable position during an

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.719
exercise that means the muscle is not

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:42.079
shortening or lengthening like it would

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:44.640
if you were going through the rest of

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:47.520
the motion something about that position

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.559
leads to added benefit over exercise

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.920
that does undergo that lengthening and

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:54.680
shortening there are multiple reasons

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.039
exercise researchers compiled the

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:59.519
evidence for isometric exercise into a

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:01.680
scientific review and covered a number

00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:04.199
of me mechanisms that could explain the

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.960
blood pressure lowering effect for one

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:09.400
isometric exercise may have an outsized

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.040
effect on a process called reactive

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.439
hyperemia in essence when the muscle is

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:16.520
stuck in one position the muscle fibers

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:19.320
and structure clamp down on the blood

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:21.840
vessels in that area this in effect

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.439
raises blood pressure quite dramatically

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.520
so unless I'm confused on which

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:28.560
direction I'm supposed to be arguing

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.320
there should be some way for that to

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.200
correct itself and better yet yet

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.759
plummet blood pressure lower than before

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.640
there is when the isometric hold is

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:41.520
released as in you move back out of the

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.640
isometric position the muscle relaxes

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.880
which also relaxes the blood vessels

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:48.560
returning blood pressure to where it was

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:50.360
before however we're not interested in

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.560
raising blood pressure and then bringing

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:55.200
it back down to where it was what good

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.640
does that do us fortunately that's not

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.600
entirely what happens the relaxation of

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.119
the muscle opens up the blood vessels

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:05.200
again and as blood rushes in it brings

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:08.720
with it oxygen nutrients and importantly

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:11.239
multiple factors like nitric oxide and

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:14.200
adenosine these bind the blood vessel

00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:17.640
wall cells called smooth muscle cells

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.680
and encourage them to relax even further

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:21.400
this opens the blood vessels even wider

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.000
dropping blood pressure beyond the

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:27.480
initial point this sudden influx of

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:30.760
blood is called hyperia but the body

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:34.280
doesn't stop there because other factors

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:36.440
also play a role your body has receptors

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:39.000
built into specific sections of the

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:42.040
heart and even some blood vessels called

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.720
B receptors these bar receptors are

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:46.040
sensitive to changes in the blood

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:48.400
pressure if there's an increase in blood

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.720
pressure like when holding an isometric

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.599
position the bar receptors will send a

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.000
signal to the brain to reduce blood

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:56.879
pressure the brain does that through

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.400
direct communication with the heart and

00:02:56.879 --> 00:03:01.319
the blood vessels via the nervous system

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:04.080
the brain encourages the heart rate to

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:06.239
fall and for blood vessels to stay open

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.680
in fact this review that we've been

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:10.519
gleaning this information from mentions

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.480
that there are studies where isometric

00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:15.799
exercise reduce heart rate and blood

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:18.440
pressure 7 hours after the exercise

00:03:15.799 --> 00:03:20.080
indicating a longstanding effect much of

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:22.159
the heart and blood pressure effects are

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.840
also confirmed including discussions of

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:28.959
the mechanisms in this systematic review

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:31.360
as well but let's go over one more such

